% M2-L11. THE MODEL WHERE THE ORDER-ENCODING LADDER IS LOAD-BEARING FOR PB LEARNING.
%
% M2-L6 measured, honestly, that every PB row this solver learned over the whole suite
% was the EMPTY CONTRADICTION -- 36 of 36 -- and gave the reason: our integer propagator
% is stronger than PB propagation on the same row, because the strength is in the order
% encoding's LADDER implications and those live in separate .opb rows (D-0028). A reason
% row handed to conflict analysis without its ladder chain usually does not PB-propagate
% the pivot the propagator legitimately deduced, so the analysis falls back before it can
% reach a useful intermediate inequality.
%
% lib/core/ladder.ml adds that chain as a row. This model is where the difference is
% visible, measured 2026-09-18 with `--stats`:
%
%     pb_ladder = true (the default)   2 conflicts, 2 rows learned, 0 fallbacks,
%                                      2 of them NON-DEGENERATE, 2 ladder rungs cited
%     pb_ladder = false (i.e. M2-L6)   2 conflicts, 0 rows learned, 2 fallbacks
%
% So the lift is load-bearing here rather than decorative: withhold the ladder rows and
% this model learns NOTHING on the PB path. test/unit/test_ladder.ml asserts exactly that
% pair of numbers through Search.config, which is the break lane -- an assertion that the
% rows appear is worth nothing without the matching one that they disappear.
%
% The shape, and why each part of it is needed:
%
%   3x1 +  x2 + 2x3 <= 4        R1
%   4x1 + 2x2 + 3x3 >= 8        R2   (written as int_lin_le with negated coefficients)
%
% R1 and R2 are jointly infeasible over these domains, and -- this is the part that makes
% the model useful rather than trivial -- BOUNDS PROPAGATION AT THE ROOT CANNOT SEE IT.
% Each row alone is satisfiable in the box and neither prunes the other into a conflict,
% so the search has to branch, which is the only way a conflict reaches PB analysis at a
% decision level at all. A root conflict is never analysed.
%
% The coefficients are deliberately NOT all equal and NOT all 1. With unit coefficients
% a reason row's pivot sits at a ladder end often enough that the bare row propagates it
% and the lift is never needed; with a coefficient of 3 against a slack of 4 it is not,
% which is the `3a + 2b <= 14` situation of the roadmap row in miniature.
%
% p and q are unconstrained 0..1 spectators, declared first, so first-fail (width 2
% against x1/x2/x3's 4 and 5) decides them ahead of the real variables -- the same device
% backjump_unsat.fzn and its M2-L10 siblings use, and for the same reason: it puts the
% real conflict below a couple of levels it does not depend on.
%
% DOMAINS ARE SINGLE DIGITS ON PURPOSE (D-0028: the order encoding is width-proportional
% and a wide domain is a proof that dwarfs the suite).
var 0..1: p;
var 0..1: q;
var 0..3: x1;
var 0..3: x2;
var 0..4: x3;
constraint int_lin_le([3,1,2],[x1,x2,x3],4);
constraint int_lin_le([-4,-2,-3],[x1,x2,x3],-8);
solve satisfy;
